# Tailscale v1.104.7: upstream's image (UPSTREAM_IMAGE, pinned by digest) with its three binaries (tailscale,
# tailscaled, containerboot) rebuilt from the release tag with two modules moved to the versions upstream's own
# v1.106.0 tag ships, and Alpine's zlib moved to the fixed package (pinned in Dockerfile.tailscale):
#   golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 -> XNET_VERSION (CVE-2026-78661, fixed in v0.62.0; upstream XNET_FIX_COMMIT on main);
#   github.com/klauspost/compress v1.20.0 -> COMPRESS_VERSION (CVE-2026-116591, fixed in v1.20.2; upstream
#   COMPRESS_FIX_COMMIT on main);
#   zlib 1.3.2-r1 -> 1.4-r0 (CVE-2026-4738).
# Upstream's v1.104.7 image fails the scan gate on those three; release-branch/1.104 had neither module change on
# 2026-11-23. The toolchain is upstream's: Tailscale's fork of Go at TS_GO_REV, the revision the tag's
# go.toolchain.rev names (Go GO_VERSION). The version stamps are upstream's, so the binaries report v1.104.7.
# WATCH_ACTION=retire: when upstream publishes a newer stable release, the weekly upstream-watch asks for a scan of
# upstream's image; if it passes the gate, consumers pin upstream's image again and this recipe is deleted.
# Bump FC_REVISION to publish a new build of the same upstream tag; an existing tag is never overwritten.
APP_NAME=tailscale
IMAGE=ghcr.io/figurecollecting/tailscale
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.tailscale
SMOKE=tailscale
WATCH_ACTION=retire
DOCS_URL=https://tailscale.com/kb/1282/docker
UPSTREAM_REPO=https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale
UPSTREAM_TAG=v1.104.7
UPSTREAM_COMMIT=cbc74fe48ef1b1649f69a4d9a602319427e25102
UPSTREAM_IMAGE=docker.io/tailscale/tailscale:v1.104.7@sha256:72c1e19e0aedca96b8533bbb0b4368564410ff20b17e53b804eb6c1f04a31be4
UPSTREAM_GO_VERSION=1.27.4
GO_VERSION=1.27.4
TS_GO_REV=1635316a95598e9fe1bff7267604daa94aa1c8ec
XNET_VERSION=v0.62.0
XNET_FIX_COMMIT=d064d751fb91fa4ffe39dad42c92862320985a0f
COMPRESS_VERSION=v1.20.2
COMPRESS_FIX_COMMIT=46f938791d5de3534179b48df7db912bc263049f
FC_REVISION=fc1
